---
title: Fiskesuppe (Creamy Norwegian Fish Soup)
description: This is a simple and delicious creamy Norwegian fish soup.
time required: 30 minutes
course: Main Course
cuisine: Norwegian
prep time: 10 minutes
source: https://scandinaviancookbook.com/fiskesuppe-creamy-norwegian-fish-soup
cook time: 20 minutes
servings: 4
tags: fish, soup
Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cF22x8pamO4
---

> You can use any type of fish except for herring, such as salmon and cod.
> Having a couple different types of fish in teh soup adds more depth to the flavor.
> The original recipe shows tiny canned shrimp, drained and rinsed.
> You can also use whichever vegetables you prefer or have already, including frozen vegetables.

Cut the @fish fillet{1%pound}(fresh or frozen) into cubes or strips. 
Crush or chop the @garlic{1%clove} and rinse the @potatoes{2%medium}, @carrots{2}, and @leek{1} and cut them into thin strips.

Heat the @butter{3%tbsp} in a #pot{} and add the garlic. Once the garlic starts to turn golden, add the @flour{5%tbsp}, whisking well.

Add the @fish stock{4 1/4%cups} and continue to whisk until there are no lumps.

Add the vegetables and @milk{1%cup} and bring to a boil. Cook for about ~{10%minutes}.

Add the @crème fraîche{1 1/4%cup}(or sour cream).
Bring the soup back to a simmer and once the soup begins to bubble again, turn off the heat.

Keep the soup on the burner and add the fish. 
Let the fish cook in the hot soup for ~{5%minutes}. 
If using @shrimp{1%cup}(optional, peeled and cooked), add right before serving.

Sprinkle with @chives{1%tbsp}(or dill or parsley) before serving.
